hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1637","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, they said: Abdul-Wahhab narrated to us. Also, Imran ibn Musa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, both of them said: Ayyub narrated to us. Also, Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Isma'il, meaning Ibn Ulayyah, narrated to us: Ayyub informed us, from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Barra', who said:

Ibn Ziyad delayed the Salah, so Abdullah ibn as-Samit came to me, and I set out a chair for him, and he sat on it. I mentioned to him what Ibn Ziyad had done, and he bit his lips, then struck his hand on my thigh and said: ""I asked Abu Dharr just as you have asked me, and he struck my thigh just as I have struck your thigh, and he said: 'I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as you have asked me, and he struck my thigh just as I have struck your thigh, and he said: ""Pray the Salah at its proper time, and if you catch it being performed with them, then pray it (again with them), and do not say: 'I have already prayed, so I will not pray (again).'""'""

This is the hadith of Bundar. Yahya ibn Hakim said: ""He bit his lips"" [with a slight variation in wording]."
